      "html": "† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">זָוִית</span>]</big>  <strong>substantivo feminino: canto</strong> (tardio) <strong>(</strong>aramaico <span dir=\"rtl\">זָוִיתָא</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܙܳܘܺܝܬܳܐ</span> (frequentemente pelo hebraico <span dir=\"rtl\">פִּנָּה</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מִקְצוֹעַ</span>), daí, como empréstimo (Frä<sup>Aramaic Fremdw. 11, 168</sup>) o árabe <span dir=\"rtl\">زَاوِيَةٌ</span> <strong>)</strong>;—plural absoluto <span dir=\"rtl\">זָוִיּוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 144:12\" href=\"/Psalms.144.12\">ψ 144:12</a>; construto <span dir=\"rtl\">זָוִיֹּת</span> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 9:15\" href=\"/Zechariah.9.15\">Zc 9:15</a>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">וּמָֽלְאוּ כַמִּזְרָק כְּזָוִיֹּת מִזְבֵּחַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 9:15\" href=\"/Zechariah.9.15\">Zc 9:15</a> símile de guerreiros banhados em sangue, v. <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 1:5\" href=\"/Leviticus.1.5\">Lv 1:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 1:11\" href=\"/Leviticus.1.11\">11</a> etc.; <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנוֹתֵינוּ כְּז׳ וגו׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 144:12\" href=\"/Psalms.144.12\">ψ 144:12</a> <em>nossas filhas como</em> (pilares de) <em>canto</em>, esculpidos (assim Che e outros, mas ver II. <a data-ref=\"BDB, חטב\" href=\"/BDB,_חטב\", dir=\"rtl\">חטב</a>) à maneira de um palácio.",
